const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"先定义什么叫企业失败",en:"Define the outcome before the predictors"},body:{zh:"研究区分破产申请与更宽的企业失败标签；后者还纳入特定退市和信用评级降至D等事件。两种标签的覆盖时期也不同。因此，破产、违约和退市不能随意互换，更不能把所有退市都视作同一种财务失败。",en:"The study distinguishes bankruptcy filings from broader failure events, including specified delistings and a D credit rating. The labels also have different historical coverage. Bankruptcy, default and delisting are not interchangeable outcomes; in particular, every delisting must not automatically be treated as the same kind of financial failure."},reference:{url:"https://dash.harvard.edu/server/api/core/bitstreams/7312037c-5bf6-6bd4-e053-0100007fdf3b/content",label:{zh:"原文定位：2005年6月27日作者稿，第1, 4–5页",en:"Source: June 27, 2005 author draft, pp. 1, 4–5"}}},{title:{zh:"观察单位是公司与月份",en:"Think in firm-month observations"},body:{zh:"作者用动态面板逻辑模型研究失败概率，每家公司可以贡献多个按月排列的观察值。问题是已知当时信息时，在指定未来期限内是否发生失败，而不是给每家公司永久贴一个标签。样本退出、时间顺序及预测期限都是模型定义的一部分。",en:"A dynamic panel logit model organizes observations by firm and month. The question is whether failure occurs over a specified future horizon given information available then, not whether a company deserves a permanent label. Exits, observation order and forecast horizon therefore belong to the definition of the model."},reference:{url:"https://dash.harvard.edu/server/api/core/bitstreams/7312037c-5bf6-6bd4-e053-0100007fdf3b/content",label:{zh:"原文定位：2005年6月27日作者稿，第4–6页",en:"Source: June 27, 2005 author draft, pp. 4–6"}}},{title:{zh:"市场口径改变了财务比率",en:"The denominator changes the financial signal"},body:{zh:"作者稿比较以账面资产缩放的盈利和负债，与使用“权益市值加账面负债”缩放的版本。后者会随股价变化，并不是把账面资产简单改名。准备变量时应分别保存分子、分母和价格日期，避免把同名的杠杆或盈利指标混在一起。",en:"The draft compares profitability and leverage scaled by book assets with versions scaled by market equity plus book liabilities. The latter changes with equity prices; it is not book assets under another name. Keep numerators, denominators and price dates separately so similarly named leverage or profitability fields are not mixed."},reference:{url:"https://dash.harvard.edu/server/api/core/bitstreams/7312037c-5bf6-6bd4-e053-0100007fdf3b/content",label:{zh:"原文定位：2005年6月27日作者稿，第5–7页",en:"Source: June 27, 2005 author draft, pp. 5–7"}}},{title:{zh:"会计数据与市场数据有不同的时钟",en:"Accounting and market inputs run on different clocks"},body:{zh:"解释变量结合季度财务、月度收益和日度价格波动。此作者稿对会计数据施加两个月的时滞，同时使用过去市场信息构造收益和波动变量。拼接时要保留各自的可用日期；固定时滞本身不能证明一份延迟披露的报表当时已可获得。",en:"Predictors combine quarterly accounts, monthly returns and daily price variability. This draft lags accounting information by two months while constructing market measures from past observations. Preserve availability dates for each input: a fixed lag does not establish that a delayed financial filing was actually accessible at that time."},reference:{url:"https://dash.harvard.edu/server/api/core/bitstreams/7312037c-5bf6-6bd4-e053-0100007fdf3b/content",label:{zh:"原文定位：2005年6月27日作者稿，第6–7页",en:"Source: June 27, 2005 author draft, pp. 6–7"}}},{title:{zh:"近期风险与远期风险不是同一道题",en:"Near and distant horizons need separate evaluation"},body:{zh:"盈利、杠杆、超额收益、波动、规模和现金等特征共同进入比较，但它们对不同期限的失败预测可能有不同作用。检验应写清未来窗口、样本基准和预测信息集。一个期限下的拟合结果不能自动成为另一期限下经过校准的概率。",en:"Profitability, leverage, excess returns, volatility, size and cash enter the comparison, but their relevance can change with the failure horizon. Evaluation needs an explicit future window, baseline and information set. A fit at one horizon does not automatically yield calibrated probabilities at another."},reference:{url:"https://dash.harvard.edu/server/api/core/bitstreams/7312037c-5bf6-6bd4-e053-0100007fdf3b/content",label:{zh:"原文定位：2005年6月27日作者稿，第2–3, 7–8页",en:"Source: June 27, 2005 author draft, pp. 2–3, 7–8"}}},{title:{zh:"失败概率与股票回报需要分开解释",en:"Failure risk is not a promised return premium"},body:{zh:"论文进一步研究财务困境与股票收益的关系，但预测企业是否失败和解释股东收益是两个不同任务。企业困境更深，并不意味着股东必然获得更高补偿；历史关系也不能转化为个股交易结论。阅读时应把失败标签与收益样本分别核对。",en:"The paper also studies stock returns, but predicting company failure and explaining shareholder payoffs are separate tasks. Greater distress need not deliver a higher reward to equity holders. Historical associations do not establish an individual-stock trade; the failure outcome and the return sample must be examined independently."},reference:{url:"https://dash.harvard.edu/server/api/core/bitstreams/7312037c-5bf6-6bd4-e053-0100007fdf3b/content",label:{zh:"原文定位：2005年6月27日作者稿，第1–3页",en:"Source: June 27, 2005 author draft, pp. 1–3"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"导读依据2005年作者稿，题录为2008年期刊版，最终设定需回到期刊原文。企业失败的标签、会计时滞与市场制度有样本依赖性，不能直接生成当前公司的违约概率。",en:"This guide uses the 2005 author draft, not the definitive specifications of the 2008 journal article. Failure labels, reporting lags and market institutions are sample-dependent; the guide does not generate current company default probabilities."}};export{e as default};
